WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.193 --> 00:00:05.123
- My name is Elvis Otieno

00:00:05.123 --> 00:00:08.405
I live in Nairobi, that's in Kenya,

00:00:08.405 --> 00:00:10.343
and I'm a country musician.

00:00:10.343 --> 00:00:12.926
("Miller's Cave" by Elvis Otieno)

00:00:12.926 --> 00:00:14.051
♫ Way down in

00:00:14.051 --> 00:00:17.301
♫ The state of Georgia

00:00:20.918 --> 00:00:21.751
One, two

00:00:22.656 --> 00:00:24.980
("Down the Road" By Elvis Otieno)

00:00:24.980 --> 00:00:27.265
♫ Down the road

00:00:27.265 --> 00:00:29.932
♫ Down the road

00:00:30.945 --> 00:00:32.626
♫ Mama wants to know

00:00:32.626 --> 00:00:34.101
♫ If I'm washed in the blood

00:00:34.101 --> 00:00:36.468
♫ Or just in the water

00:00:36.468 --> 00:00:38.160
♫ Daddy wants to know

00:00:38.160 --> 00:00:42.327
♫ If I make enough to take his daughter

00:00:43.734 --> 00:00:45.919
Country music was my first love.

00:00:45.919 --> 00:00:48.371
My parents, I think, looking back at it

00:00:48.371 --> 00:00:53.082
were very unique in a way
because they loved country music.

00:00:53.082 --> 00:00:54.404
They had all the records,

00:00:54.404 --> 00:00:56.430
and I listened to all the beautiful music

00:00:56.430 --> 00:00:57.485
that was there.

00:00:57.485 --> 00:00:59.923
That, kind of like, shaped up the person

00:00:59.923 --> 00:01:02.674
that I was to become later in my life.

00:01:02.674 --> 00:01:06.174
We identify quite a lot with country music

00:01:07.025 --> 00:01:09.235
because of the message that is in it.

00:01:09.235 --> 00:01:11.318
Family, love, heartbreak.

00:01:12.718 --> 00:01:14.199
("Me And Bobby Mcgee" by Elvis Otieno)

00:01:14.199 --> 00:01:16.436
♫ From the coal mines of Kentucky

00:01:16.436 --> 00:01:19.769
♫ To the California sun

00:01:21.598 --> 00:01:24.621
I draw a lot of inspirations
from different singers,

00:01:24.621 --> 00:01:26.592
and different songwriters.

00:01:26.592 --> 00:01:27.831
Garth Brooks, Charley Pride, Alan Jackson,

00:01:27.831 --> 00:01:30.533
Don Williams, George
Strait, Brooks and Dunn.

00:01:30.533 --> 00:01:32.865
The list is endless.

00:01:32.865 --> 00:01:37.275
The struggles they experienced
are really universal.

00:01:37.275 --> 00:01:38.402
("One More Day" by Elvis Otieno)

00:01:38.402 --> 00:01:40.495
♫ One more day

00:01:40.495 --> 00:01:43.162
♫ One more time

00:01:44.044 --> 00:01:47.014
Every time I've gone on
stage, I have to make sure

00:01:47.014 --> 00:01:50.653
my audience are with me,
and they get my message.

00:01:50.653 --> 00:01:54.003
And, usually what I want them to feel,

00:01:54.003 --> 00:01:56.503
is the raw emotions of a song.

00:01:59.761 --> 00:02:02.038
♫ Sad they start with me

00:02:02.038 --> 00:02:06.205
♫ As I walk the streets of my memories

00:02:07.350 --> 00:02:10.880
I'm just like a vessel, but through me,

00:02:10.880 --> 00:02:14.963
they can feel the emotions
and it has to be real,

00:02:15.973 --> 00:02:18.556
it has to come from your heart.

00:02:22.195 --> 00:02:24.989
Thank you, thank you so much.

00:02:24.989 --> 00:02:26.989
(chime)

